{"game": "alien-swarm", "language": "english", "appid": 630, "month": "2026-06", "window": 1, "start_date": 1780272000, "end_date": 1782863999, "month_true_total": 17, "quota": 17, "returned": 17, "pulled_at": "2026-10-06 01:12:17 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "229268320", "author": {"steamid": "76561199278932607", "personaname": "ugh zan 3 HD", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199278932607/", "num_games_owned": 10, "num_reviews": 12, "playtime_forever": 275, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 161, "last_played": 1787043578, "avatar": "942b271ffff3251d7fc2598d03602adb5421c21a"}, "language": "english", "review": "this games is SOO Fun one of the best game i play", "timestamp_created": 1782847474, "timestamp_updated": 1782847474, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 1, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1279569600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "229252733", "author": {"steamid": "76561199786706752", "personaname": "Lilie The Sea D.", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199786706752/", "num_games_owned": 3, "num_reviews": 4, "playtime_forever": 129, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 129, "last_played": 1752933815, "avatar": "5a86545f3e6a1971e90eab40091d02096cb9781d"}, "language": "english", "review": "Why Alien Swarm Is Forgettable\n\nLet's be honest. Most people didn't install Alien Swarm because they were excited to play Alien Swarm. They installed it because it gave a free TF2 hat. That's the game's entire legacy. Ask most TF2 players what they remember about Alien Swarm, and the answer is usually: \"The game that gave me a hat.\" Not the missions. Not the characters. Not the gameplay. The hat.\n\nAnd honestly, that's completely deserved, because outside of that reward, Alien Swarm doesn't really do anything special. It's a top-down co-op shooter. That's it. There are countless games in that genre, and most of them are more memorable. Alien Swarm doesn't have an amazing story, it doesn't have iconic characters, it doesn't have revolutionary gameplay, and it certainly doesn't have enough content to keep most people interested for very long. Nothing about it stands out.\n\nThe funniest part is how hard the game tried to push the whole \"play with your friends\" idea. The TF2 hat achievement was clearly designed to make players convince somebody else to install the game. Except people immediately started looking for ways to bypass that requirement because nobody actually wanted to play Alien Swarm. They wanted the hat. The game was just standing in the way.\n\nI'm leaving this here so you don't play this piece of ♥♥♥♥ with any of your friends: \n\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1981094150\n\nSo instead of creating a community, the entire conversation became:\n\n\"How do I get the hat as fast as possible?\"\n\nNot:\n\n\"How do I get better at Alien Swarm?\"\n\nNot:\n\n\"What's the best strategy?\"\n\nNot:\n\n\"Who wants to play tonight?\"\n\nJust:\n\n\"How fast can I get the reward and uninstall this thing?\"\n\nThat says everything you need to know.\n\nPeople weren't interested in the game. They were interested in what the game was bribing them with. Alien Swarm became less of a game and more of a requirement. An obstacle. A chore you complete before collecting your cosmetic item.\n\nAnd that's the biggest problem. Alien Swarm feels less like a game people genuinely wanted to play and more like a promotional campaign that accidentally came bundled with a video game. You install it, get the achievement, claim the hat, and never think about it again.\n\nThere are games that create communities. There are games that leave lasting memories. There are games people still talk about years later because they were genuinely fun. Alien Swarm isn't one of them. For most players, it exists for one reason and one reason only: a free TF2 cosmetic.\n\nThe game's greatest achievement wasn't creating a fanbase. It was convincing people to tolerate it long enough to unlock a hat.\n\nThat's not a legacy. That's a giveaway.\n\nAlien Swarm isn't memorable. It isn't unique. It isn't special. It's the gaming equivalent of a coupon. You redeem it once, get what you came for, and throw it away.\n\nIt's a one-time trick. And it wasn't even a good one.\n\nIt's just:\n\n\"Play this game. Get a hat. Leave.\"\n\nAnd that's exactly what most people did.", "timestamp_created": 1782835333, "timestamp_updated": 1782837515, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 3, "weighted_vote_score": "0.368098169565200806", "comment_count": 2, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1279569600", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 28, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "229167845", "author": {"steamid": "76561198829216861", "personaname": "Aymane", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/umutardabenli/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 194, "playtime_forever": 89, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 89, "last_played": 1782422967, "avatar": "76c2c57990ae1af551df7337b66debf3946cccbc"}, "language": "english", "review": "It feels like a flop when it's not, obviously it's a standalone tech demo that has been officially abandoned. but it's actually fun and it at least deserves a workshop update so players can keep this game more alive", "timestamp_created": 1782751957, "timestamp_updated": 1782751957, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 11, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.671979069709777832", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_e